# Project guidance

Purpose: maintain an independent Python project using the **{{ profile }}** profile.

Commands: `uv sync --all-groups`; `uv run ruff format --check .`; `uv run ruff check .`; `uv run mypy src`; `uv run pytest`.

Search before reading: locate relevant files and tests first, then read the smallest useful set.

{% if profile == "minimal" -%}
Architecture invariants: keep the `src/` layout direct and do not add layers until a concrete requirement needs them. Keep dependencies minimal and do not add a runtime dependency on AgentReady.
{% elif profile == "application" -%}
Architecture invariants: preserve `main`/bootstrap → application → domain; domain stays independent of application code and frameworks. Keep dependencies minimal and do not add a runtime dependency on AgentReady.
{% else -%}
Architecture invariants: preserve entrypoint/bootstrap → application → domain; adapters depend inward and bootstrap owns composition. Keep dependencies minimal and do not add a runtime dependency on AgentReady.
{% endif -%}

Minimum coherent diff: make the smallest change that satisfies the acceptance criteria and avoid speculative directories, abstractions, or refactors.

Verification: run the documented commands relevant to the change, then the full baseline before merging.

Definition of done: behavior is tested, formatting/lint/types/tests pass, and the diff is focused.

Start with [agent guidance index](docs/agent/index.md). Project work is tracked under `docs/work/`.

For implementation work, select one READY item, use its Type to choose the workflow in `docs/agent/index.md`, read its normative specification and only relevant standards, preserve requirements, update the implementation record and documentation impact, then sync the registry and changelog. If blocked, record why, mark BLOCKED, and stop.
